      "q": "Solve by Cramer's rule: $3x+2y=12$, $x-y=-1$. Give the value of $y$.",
      "answer": 3,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "solution": "$\\Delta=\\begin{vmatrix}3&2\\\\1&-1\\end{vmatrix}=-5$, $\\Delta_y=\\begin{vmatrix}3&12\\\\1&-1\\end{vmatrix}=-15$.\n\n$y=\\dfrac{\\Delta_y}{\\Delta}=3$ (and $x=2$)."
