      "type": "numeric",
      "marks": 3,
      "q": "Solve by Gaussian elimination: $x+y+z=6$, $x+2y+3z=14$, $x+4y+9z=36$. Give the value of $z$.",
      "answer": 3,
      "tolerance": 0,
      "solution": "Subtract the first equation from the others: $y+2z=8$ and $3y+8z=30$.\n\nThen $3(8-2z)+8z=30$ gives $z=3$, so $y=2$ and $x=1$."
